Generate images locally with AUTOMATIC1111 Stable Diffusion WebUI on Raspberry Pi 5-class hardware.

CPU-only image generation with an optional graphical launcher. The installer offers four optional checkpoints: CyberRealistic V7.0, Realistic Vision V5.1 Inpainting, Realistic Vision V6.0 New Vision B1, and Real Dream 16.

Requires aarch64, Raspberry Pi 5/500/Compute Module 5, and at least 4 GiB reported RAM. Raspberry Pi OS 64-bit is the target environment; other accepted boards/OS combinations need recorded testing. Generation can be slow on a CPU. The model selection totals approximately 10.66 GB with all four enabled, excluding dependencies, temporary files, and installation backups.

To run with the optional menu launcher: Menu -> Graphics -> Stable Diffusion
To run in a terminal with the default installation location: ~/run_sd.sh
For a custom installation location, run its run_sd.sh instead.

Run LAN mode with internet access once for initial setup. Offline mode skips dependency setup but still listens on the network. No authentication is configured by the launcher; use a trusted network.

Pi-Apps updates and removal retain models, outputs, extensions, settings, and added or modified files. Updates need room for a second installation while rollback backups exist. Close the GUI and stop WebUI before updating. Installation uses interactive terminal menus; unattended installation is not supported.
